/* ============================================================================
   THE KIT AND SERVICES CATALOGUE: the 2027 rate card, filed so it can be found
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Generated from "WIP - EP Team - Rate Card - MASTER.xlsx", tab "2027 - Rate
   Card Services" (352 rows). The sheet's own column B is a DEPARTMENT, not a
   shelf: a cone, a TMP fee, cable ties and a Pitagone caliper all sat under
   "Traffic Management". So every row carries three things:

     - `category`: where you would look for it (one, fixed list below).
     - `depts`: the sheet's departments, kept as a filter. Seventeen items were
       listed under two departments; they are one row here with two tags.
     - `family` / `variant`: sizes and versions of one thing (hi-vis S..5XL,
       traffic light 2..5 head) shown as one line with a size picker.

   Folded rather than duplicated: rows that ARE an existing seeded charge (the
   750mm cone, Heras panel, tower light, B2B radio, charge dock, TMP, crew
   transport, welfare unit, hi-vis) only lend that charge their name as an
   alias. Labour rows on the HVM block (HVM Steward, Traffic Manager...) are
   people and belong on the labour card, so they are not here.

   KIT OR SERVICE (5 Nov 2026). Anything you can touch is kit, even when it
   comes with a driver or is installed: Shuttle Vehicle, Private Bus Shuttle,
   Top Banner Branding and Letter Drop Printing moved to kit; Line Marking -
   Manual (a crew doing the work) moved to services. Ids kept, so old quotes
   still resolve; their old codes (TRN-003/004/006, ONS-002/004, TRF-010) are
   retired, not reused.

   PLACEHOLDER RATES (27 Oct 2026). Every row the sheet left unpriced now
   carries an invented rate, flagged `placeholderRate: true`, so the picker can
   be used end to end. They are NOT EP's prices. Replace them in the Table of
   charges; grep `placeholderRate` to find what is still made up.

   PRICES (as imported). The sheet is a WIP: only 16 rows have a figure in the Rate A/B/C
   charge columns. Everything else is `charge: 0` = NO RATE YET, and is shown
   in the picker but cannot be added (see `hasRate` in lib/charges.ts) until
   Finance prices it in the Table of charges. "Planning" and front/back-end
   development have figures that are hourly; a service cannot be hourly here,
   so they wait for a rate too rather than be billed per job at £40.
   ========================================================================== */

